<problem><title>Video review questions</title>
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />

<p>Which of the equations below is a differential equation?</p>

<answer name="ans1a">
  <choice><m>f(t) = 3t^2 + 2t - 7</m></choice>
  <choice credit="1"><m>3t + 6 = \frac{dx}{dt}</m></choice>
  <choice><m>f(t) = 3e^{-2t}</m></choice>
</answer>
</exercise>
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>How can you check to see that a proposed solution to a differential eqation is correct?</p>
<answer name="ans1b">
  <choice credit="1">Differentiate the solution to check whether it matches the original differential equation</choice>
  <choice>Invert the solution to check whether it matches the differential equation</choice>
  <choice>Think of at least five other solutions and then roll a six sided dice to choose one</choice>
  <choice>Take the limit of the solution as <m>t</m> goes to infinity and check to see whether it matches the differential equation.</choice>
</answer>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>Which of the following equations provides the <alert>general solution</alert> to the differential equation <m>\frac{dx}{dt} = 15</m> ?</p>
<answer name="ans1c">
  <choice><m>x(t) = 15t</m></choice>
  <choice><m>x(t) = 15t + 130</m></choice>
  <choice credit="1"><m>x(t) = 15t + C</m></choice>
  <choice><m>f(t) = 0</m></choice>
</answer>
</exercise>
</problem>
  
</section>
